Example rules, in priority order (they show the syntax; they are not a good schedule for this system):
```
{"condition": "enabled & s = 2", "action": "u2_grant_drive"}
{"condition": "shortcuts_left = 0 & enabled", "action": "any"}
{"condition": "X_PCT >= 50 & s1 = 3", "action": "u1_use"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "u2_ready"}
```
Rule 1 grants drive to user 2 whenever that is possible while the arbiter serves user 2. Rule 2, once the arbiter's shortcut can no longer happen, allows every action that is possible. Rule 3 lets user 1 use its resource when users keep resources at least half the time. The last rule is a catch-all default.
